@startuml credentials-http-api-sequence
title Credential Registry HTTP API - PQS-backed Reads
hide footbox

actor Client
participant "Java / Registry\nHTTP API" as API
database "PQS / PostgreSQL" as PQS
participant "Canton Participant" as Canton

== Continuous PQS indexing ==
Canton -> PQS: Continuously index visible contracts
note over Canton,PQS
  PQS owns ledger synchronization, restart recovery,
  and interface projections.

  The registry API does not run a custom ledger-ingestion
  or event-indexing pipeline.
end note

== Single lookup ==
Client -> API: GET /api/v1/credentials/{credentialId}
API -> PQS: Prepared SQL joining active(Credential) and\nactive(RegisteredCredential) on contract ID,\nfiltered by logical credential ID
PQS --> API: Zero, one, or multiple associated rows
API --> Client: 404, 200, or 409

== Bounded bulk page ==
Client -> API: GET /api/v1/credentials?page=0&pageSize=50
API -> API: Validate zero-based page and positive pageSize
API -> PQS: JOIN active interface projections on contract ID\nORDER BY logical ID, contract ID\nLIMIT pageSize + 1 OFFSET page * pageSize
PQS --> API: Bounded associated rows
API --> Client: items, page, pageSize, hasNext
note over Client,PQS
  page is zero-based.
  pageSize is the maximum number of returned items.
  Offset pagination is eventually consistent with PQS.
  Concurrent changes can shift page boundaries.
  No snapshot guarantee is claimed.
end note

note over API,PQS
  An optional narrow payload index MAY accelerate lookup
  when supported by the deployed PQS version. It does not
  change the projection or ingestion architecture.
end note

@enduml
